A go.work at the root, scanned from the root. TestScanFindsParentWorkspace scans the same archive
from services/ instead, where the workspace is a directory above and go searches for it.

Reading only <root>/go.work would report svc as outside a workspace that names it — the same
conflation the Repo type exists to prevent, arrived at from the other direction.

The root is not itself a module, so ./... reaches nothing at all there: "directory prefix . does
not contain modules listed in go.work or their selected dependencies".

modules_on_disk: 1
go_list_m: 1
go_list_dotdotdot: 0
discovered_modules: 1
discovered_packages: 1
packages_with_tests: 0
has_workspace: 1
modules_in_workspace: 1
-- go.work --
go 1.27

use ./services/svc
-- services/svc/go.mod --
module parent.test/svc

go 1.27
-- services/svc/svc.go --
package svc

func S() int { return 1 }
